# Project Context: Self-hosted Postgres + Better Auth

## Core Objective
CMUD / MedLearHub runs on local/self-hosted PostgreSQL and Better Auth. Do not reintroduce Supabase clients or Auth.

## Architecture
- **Auth:** Better Auth (`src/lib/auth.ts`, `src/lib/auth-client.ts`). Server guards: `src/lib/require-auth.ts` (`requireAuth`).
- **Env:** `src/lib/env.ts` — requires `DATABASE_URL`, `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET`, `BETTER_AUTH_URL`; optional `BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS`.
- **Database:** `DATABASE_URL` + `pg` (`src/lib/db.ts`). CMS schema: `scripts/schema-cms-local.sql`.
- **Media:** Local `/public/media/` and `/public/attachment/` with relative paths in the DB.
- **CMS data:** Always from Postgres via server functions — not from `public/cms/*.json` at runtime.
- **Zod:** Pinned to `4.4.3` (Better Auth `.meta()` compatibility). Use `overrides` — do not downgrade to Zod 3.
- **Deploy:** Nitro preset `node-server` only (`vite.config.ts`). Start with `npm start` / PM2 (`ecosystem.config.cjs`). Do not use Cloudflare/Wrangler for this self-host path.

## Guardrails
- Do not add `@supabase/supabase-js` or `supabase.from(...)` calls.
- Prefer local relative media paths (`/media/...`, `/attachment/...`).
- Keep the Lovable-connected branch working; avoid force-push / history rewrite.

<!-- LOVABLE:BEGIN -->
> [!IMPORTANT]
> This project is connected to [Lovable](https://lovable.dev). Avoid rewriting
> published git history — force pushing, or rebasing/amending/squashing commits
> that are already pushed — as it rewrites history on Lovable's side and the
> user will likely lose their project history.
>
> Commits you push to the connected branch sync back to Lovable and show up in
> the editor, so keep the branch in a working state.
